> A hand-checkable calculation

One lambda-return step with reward1, discount.9, lambda.5, next critic4 and next return6 gives5.5. The actual experiment computes all three gradient sets before applying model, actor and critic updates.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dreamer_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double>values{1+.9*((1-.5)*4+.5*6)};std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("dreamer worked calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/dreamer_worked.svg");}
